#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133489 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d893f937-d802-5d27-b91a-b78caee0313e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "0ab996ae-e3a7-5353-87c2-9b2a01f4f808" :question/math-academy-id "e-5538" :question/problem "Given ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/assets/eec8345a2a1eb622aafae6890c6548efcd5b595d18334b5bad9e43f8b0fd4534.png) find $\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{50} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133490 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff66eef8-74b6-5553-af34-7da5a8cbbb02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "f2ff1620-28e1-59ba-97ca-c43f3f300fdf" :question/math-academy-id "e-5539" :question/problem "Given the vectors ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/assets/c3261bc45f978551da6b9ae98489e4eeceadfb5a4669a703736b3d623ed2c41d.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/assets/40f7e2f6c5aaff24c18d65776fbbb62f44effeb921bc6e54a4e4f7ada905e614.png) find the distance $\\text{d}(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y}).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the distance, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1-2)^{2}+(2-0)^{2}+(3-(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+4+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133491 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae41d849-9def-540c-8985-8fbeec679991" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "7b7adf29-1653-5de7-915c-80a09f05995a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5540" :question/problem "Normalize the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/assets/33fcf438acd77616d7f5c6881234f9dcc87136575b741af6af72eee9d4401dfb.png)" :question/worked-solution "To normalize a vector $\\mathbf{x},$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\dfrac{\\mathbf{x}}{\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|}.$ Therefore, to normalize $\\mathbf{x},$ we first calculate $\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $\\mathbf{x}$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-8}{10} \\\\ \\frac{6}{10}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133562 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "837e0fa4-b8d3-59c1-87c7-44317adafaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Constant Out of the Norm"}] :question/id #uuid "86cf381d-8a69-5290-806b-09477c7ff92e" :question/math-academy-id "e-6190" :question/problem "If $\\left\\Vert {- \\dfrac{ \\mathbf{x} }{2} } \\right\\Vert = 5,$ find $\\Vert 3 \\mathbf{x} \\Vert.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n\\Vert k \\mathbf{x} \\Vert= \\vert k \\vert \\cdot \\Vert \\mathbf{x} \\Vert\n$$\n\nUsing this fact, we can solve for the norm $\\Vert x \\Vert$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-\\frac{x}{2}‖ & =5 \\\\ ‖-\\frac{1}{2}x‖ & =5 \\\\ |-\\frac{1}{2}|\\cdot ‖x‖ & =5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ‖x‖ & =5 \\\\ ‖x‖ & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $\\Vert 3 \\mathbf{x} \\Vert \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖3x‖ & =3\\cdot ‖x‖ \\\\  & =3\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323488 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d893f937-d802-5d27-b91a-b78caee0313e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2306eaeb-f186-5328-a8b4-ec163a12337e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323490} {:answer/id #uuid "68361fa6-ca9a-54e1-b147-a48dca9d9149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323491} {:answer/id #uuid "afaaf6b3-3235-53b5-9fef-f76b5615ef7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323492} {:answer/id #uuid "070173d0-73b3-5f0a-b278-756905f44aab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323493} {:answer/id #uuid "2c405deb-1d8a-5c5c-baf3-d090d33fb8d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afaaf6b3-3235-53b5-9fef-f76b5615ef7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323492} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e0a8f54-3922-55bc-95aa-41c9440c988d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323489}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1324bd91-70ba-57b8-a698-199123711535" :question/math-academy-id "q-139961" :question/problem "Given $x=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖x‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323495 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff66eef8-74b6-5553-af34-7da5a8cbbb02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a851a74-9c3f-50a9-9640-b05037907231" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323497} {:answer/id #uuid "c17de667-1f07-5bb3-bac9-47627f057063" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323498} {:answer/id #uuid "860cb02f-486f-58fa-835a-3cb273279687" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323499} {:answer/id #uuid "ec52e87d-42b1-56ec-96ec-3836c4ca4baa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323500} {:answer/id #uuid "c5870435-4844-5067-b7f9-57cc6f3bba75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "860cb02f-486f-58fa-835a-3cb273279687" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323499} :answer-field/id #uuid "2217fd42-5a46-567e-be3f-b655477772c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323496}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "13ad3892-e70d-51a7-8479-806d0e4aae8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-139963" :question/problem "Given the vectors $x=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$, find the distance $\\text{d}(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(10-4)^{2}+(4-(-4))^{2}+(2-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{8}^{2}+(0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+64+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323502 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff66eef8-74b6-5553-af34-7da5a8cbbb02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39defc9e-3697-55ba-a6f1-73c8dca8ee57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323504} {:answer/id #uuid "ed7fcf95-712d-55e1-b114-71640009cc01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323505} {:answer/id #uuid "f3d82a91-f7bd-5ca3-a58b-5080143de17e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323506} {:answer/id #uuid "a26eb872-4aaf-5d79-9af3-e4c60721af56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323507} {:answer/id #uuid "ddcce557-eef9-50d0-b0ae-0caa00868d38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed7fcf95-712d-55e1-b114-71640009cc01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323505} :answer-field/id #uuid "33edf0b8-363d-5901-ae07-bef2a1b1fd11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "54d27d47-3382-571c-bf42-d8a07c9fce45" :question/math-academy-id "q-139964" :question/problem "Given the vectors $a=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, find the distance $\\text{d}(a,b).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(a,b) & =‖a-b‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({a}_{1}-{b}_{1})^{2}+({a}_{2}-{b}_{2})^{2}+({a}_{3}-{b}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5-3)^{2}+(0-1)^{2}+(3-(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+1+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{81} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323509 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "837e0fa4-b8d3-59c1-87c7-44317adafaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Constant Out of the Norm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72b97cd5-3410-51c5-b03b-8cf8c5dff801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323511} {:answer/id #uuid "89c27295-afa5-5c11-a43f-e4c7dd5539e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323512} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb19415-a52b-5a39-8a54-ff19139e596a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323513} {:answer/id #uuid "d34039fa-4f8c-5ad4-92e5-b30edd590533" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323514} {:answer/id #uuid "891c35eb-8137-59a2-be58-e3ef9902b635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d34039fa-4f8c-5ad4-92e5-b30edd590533" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323514} :answer-field/id #uuid "78f67838-6a50-5f11-bc90-936c31694e63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323510}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "16a1d67f-1c2e-5d0c-80e7-048c3fd5b49a" :question/math-academy-id "q-139968" :question/problem "If $‖5x‖=4$, find $‖-10x‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n‖kx‖=|k|\\cdot ‖x‖\n$$\n\nUsing this fact, we can solve for the norm $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖5x‖ & =4 \\\\ |5|\\cdot ‖x‖ & =4 \\\\ ‖x‖ & =\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $‖-10x‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-10x‖ & =|-10|\\cdot ‖x‖ \\\\  & =10\\cdot ‖x‖ \\\\  & =10\\cdot \\frac{4}{5} \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d893f937-d802-5d27-b91a-b78caee0313e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5469215-e5bd-5742-a93f-721ac5238e98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131199} {:answer/id #uuid "ac4dd618-8b90-5642-b540-39001f644b08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131200} {:answer/id #uuid "d21e4d29-a260-5b4f-ac0d-5456fcac6615" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131201} {:answer/id #uuid "e0d152d5-8b44-565f-b287-186af63200cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131202} {:answer/id #uuid "758366a3-c2f6-5425-adec-1c0ed1b00707" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0d152d5-8b44-565f-b287-186af63200cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131202} :answer-field/id #uuid "276a922c-7135-5a79-97bb-4fcf310a1387" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131198}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5828f6e3-0ddc-5915-957d-8070ad1bd7f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-39212" :question/problem "Given $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖x‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134129 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d893f937-d802-5d27-b91a-b78caee0313e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "834ee9dc-0ca7-53ea-bffb-b576ac50c08f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131217} {:answer/id #uuid "f71925ca-42c8-53a9-8132-9504916f6f5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131218} {:answer/id #uuid "14131f7f-4621-5259-be21-beeaf45409c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131219} {:answer/id #uuid "2e7eea0a-784e-586b-874e-c8753a59da7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131220} {:answer/id #uuid "66294ba2-bde7-52c9-abd3-bc045edb7745" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{29}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f71925ca-42c8-53a9-8132-9504916f6f5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131218} :answer-field/id #uuid "93efb215-afea-5b41-93ef-450da5f84e35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9daa26a9-dacd-58c0-9293-05262c472ad6" :question/math-academy-id "q-39238" :question/problem "Given $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖a‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖a‖ & =\\sqrt{{a}_{1}^{2}+{a}_{2}^{2}+{a}_{3}^{2}+{a}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323516 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff66eef8-74b6-5553-af34-7da5a8cbbb02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72ed4de6-b6e0-5e4e-971f-992801f8c771" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323518} {:answer/id #uuid "9d27d045-bffa-58ec-8ed2-6015a874a7ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323519} {:answer/id #uuid "cdd2e7a9-8562-5ed0-a6ab-683e734d48eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323520} {:answer/id #uuid "ab86ad56-d8fd-568f-89ed-a04301ed6479" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{59}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323521} {:answer/id #uuid "9c0089c3-9a70-5e4e-bc36-23c641534703" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab86ad56-d8fd-568f-89ed-a04301ed6479" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{59}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323521} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab4e500a-ddc7-5e7c-8667-1d8f8b15a351" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323517}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9e745c81-2b0d-52f3-bc63-3a111cb350f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-39243" :question/problem "Given the vectors $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$, find the distance $\\text{d}(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1-4)^{2}+(3-(-2))^{2}+(-2-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+25+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{59}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae41d849-9def-540c-8985-8fbeec679991" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d9d06ec-ca55-5421-b1b6-60de33ba0caf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131235} {:answer/id #uuid "9c671771-073c-5586-b141-222bcfaf1126" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131236} {:answer/id #uuid "d739a0d9-28c6-548e-8fe4-ae095c1ada32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131237} {:answer/id #uuid "f08a5b92-21d5-577f-be7d-8b293619e7cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131238} {:answer/id #uuid "1615df75-de02-5910-8db5-acdaf84452e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1615df75-de02-5910-8db5-acdaf84452e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131239} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bffa711-163c-50d6-8021-3941f57539e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131234}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a350f3a1-cd41-5360-9252-b46fc873edab" :question/math-academy-id "q-39244" :question/problem "Normalize the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "To normalize a vector $x,$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\frac{x}{‖x‖}.$ Therefore, to normalize $x,$ we first calculate $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+1+4+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $x$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{-1}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{-2}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323523 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff66eef8-74b6-5553-af34-7da5a8cbbb02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7c36d6a-6285-569a-8fd3-2aa0eb0477c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323525} {:answer/id #uuid "39cbda01-d4d0-5c95-ac27-8686465c0b8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{445}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323526} {:answer/id #uuid "3aeebf3e-74d0-54a0-a35d-c3c94d9d1932" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{482}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323527} {:answer/id #uuid "757be661-3fd6-52d4-a1b1-fe69e6cf668a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323528} {:answer/id #uuid "6e5de87f-bda7-5716-889c-2e751df7b96a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "757be661-3fd6-52d4-a1b1-fe69e6cf668a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323528} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ca478d2-7dfe-5f84-b65c-230855d1d564" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "82881693-9429-5847-a8a3-7d89b318500b" :question/math-academy-id "q-39761" :question/problem "Find the distance between the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $0.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,0) & =‖x-0‖ \\\\  & =‖x‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(20)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16+400+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{441} \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323530 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "837e0fa4-b8d3-59c1-87c7-44317adafaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Constant Out of the Norm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "120e40a1-0ecc-555a-a96f-b42f27f1faa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "972" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323532} {:answer/id #uuid "79b4b5fe-505a-555e-a666-e37572db7fe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "144\\sqrt{213}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323533} {:answer/id #uuid "f23249e8-0d21-53b4-9e24-36e2fa050249" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,296" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323534} {:answer/id #uuid "1e5b13f9-6186-572f-a41b-6b6cfc088aef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "432\\sqrt{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323535} {:answer/id #uuid "28657921-240d-565f-912c-089878d2d350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f23249e8-0d21-53b4-9e24-36e2fa050249" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,296" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323534} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e37e228-a78b-5165-8741-dab3f0d78fe6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323531}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7c79b45c-ccf1-5435-9a0b-cd68b68b15b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-39770" :question/problem "Given the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{12} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖144x‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n‖kx‖=|k|\\cdot ‖x‖\n$$\n\nUsing this fact and the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖144x‖ & =|144|‖x‖ \\\\  & =144\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(\\sqrt{12})^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =144\\sqrt{64+4+12+1} \\\\  & =144\\sqrt{81} \\\\  & =144\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =1\\,296.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae41d849-9def-540c-8985-8fbeec679991" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4c5ae8e-300a-5d7c-aa32-93d7a7a146ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm \\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323539} {:answer/id #uuid "44a73934-239d-5ee4-a24a-c144e8aaa375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323540} {:answer/id #uuid "a59afa8c-fa38-5477-8f44-3cdc0fb56bd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm \\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323541} {:answer/id #uuid "408952fd-d9fa-5269-9971-35af17a9735f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323542} {:answer/id #uuid "951c68a3-c15d-5dd8-bb39-c8257da85daa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4c5ae8e-300a-5d7c-aa32-93d7a7a146ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm \\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323539} :answer-field/id #uuid "e33833f9-70cb-5f3b-aa4f-07f0c54fe178" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323538}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4825ebc-e078-543f-a174-111e5aa6d9a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-39862" :question/problem "Find $k$, if $u=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9} \\\\ \\frac{k}{9} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{8}{9}\\end{aligned}]$ is a unit vector." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the norm of the vector $x$ in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u‖ & =\\sqrt{{u}_{1}^{2}+{u}_{2}^{2}+{u}_{3}^{2}+{u}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{9})}^{2}+{(\\frac{k}{9})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+{(\\frac{8}{9})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{81}+\\frac{{k}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{64}{81}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{74+{k}^{2}}{81}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given equation  $‖u‖=1,$ we obtain an equation that we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{74+{k}^{2}}{81}} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{74+{k}^{2}} & =9 \\\\ {(\\sqrt{74+{k}^{2}})}^{2} & ={9}^{2} \\\\ 74+{k}^{2} & =81 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =7 \\\\ k & =\\pm \\sqrt{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323544 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d893f937-d802-5d27-b91a-b78caee0313e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "920fa0d6-13fb-5fa4-beb0-fa449ed72e99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{39}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323546} {:answer/id #uuid "8443b664-9ac2-53b5-ab0e-21fdc83b41a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323547} {:answer/id #uuid "8f798e79-e653-5497-acc6-3b8b1d1e13a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323548} {:answer/id #uuid "bdf50421-be11-5790-bca1-d28024aa1eb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323549} {:answer/id #uuid "3ea350b6-97cd-55ee-a2c1-1fef53166382" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323550}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f798e79-e653-5497-acc6-3b8b1d1e13a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323548} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae46620c-8477-598f-8414-dab68b478f1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323545}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "37066500-2d94-5224-a314-6b14626bbe07" :question/math-academy-id "q-74114" :question/problem "Given $d=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖d‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖d‖ & =\\sqrt{{d}_{1}^{2}+{d}_{2}^{2}+{d}_{3}^{2}+{d}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+1+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323551 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d893f937-d802-5d27-b91a-b78caee0313e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e2678b7-2b69-5781-863b-513f90c895ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323553} {:answer/id #uuid "b0d003fe-0111-5f45-98d7-c959c445f1d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323554} {:answer/id #uuid "1359199f-07e6-545f-b427-1766dc1fd1fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323555} {:answer/id #uuid "ce2eb5e1-fcfb-553b-a525-1bc010812ac1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323556} {:answer/id #uuid "120ddf20-3466-5be4-8d59-b146530a2fc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0d003fe-0111-5f45-98d7-c959c445f1d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323554} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ba325b2-8ab6-5bed-9504-c2b71fa76ee4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323552}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc278b4c-d5e0-59af-8abe-29b909de52fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-74117" :question/problem "Given $v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖v‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}+{v}_{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+1+1+4+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff66eef8-74b6-5553-af34-7da5a8cbbb02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95617a0f-4c20-53ce-8190-1f67c3b251a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323560} {:answer/id #uuid "f6d04160-294e-5be8-a838-a7e3041ccc0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323561} {:answer/id #uuid "410eb186-3b3a-51ba-ab08-61008a6ce737" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323562} {:answer/id #uuid "424037a9-3673-5b58-ad51-e7bcd8517de6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323563} {:answer/id #uuid "bef3ee35-b1f4-5ad4-a78c-dc1e0f7cc82c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "424037a9-3673-5b58-ad51-e7bcd8517de6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323563} :answer-field/id #uuid "705c62b2-ff41-5893-aaf2-cfb9558c5176" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323559}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4d8b0dcb-912b-5bc9-9e9c-8f6ccb5733fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-74126" :question/problem "Find the distance between the vector $c=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{7}\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $0.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(c,0) & =‖c-0‖ \\\\  & =‖c‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{c}_{1}^{2}+{c}_{2}^{2}+{c}_{3}^{2}+{c}_{4}^{2}+{c}_{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(\\sqrt{7})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+0+4+16+7} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323565 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "837e0fa4-b8d3-59c1-87c7-44317adafaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Constant Out of the Norm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56794519-0dee-50a8-935c-31daa21c8d60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323567} {:answer/id #uuid "ee14b9d5-037a-5652-8791-be4a55fcb418" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323568} {:answer/id #uuid "18116f1e-1e22-5107-8cb5-4b60bd3a4283" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323569} {:answer/id #uuid "1d5fe6d2-2232-5b24-b0fa-9bad7554a445" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323570} {:answer/id #uuid "6b587d60-3948-5f29-bd42-e7b8dc2229be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18116f1e-1e22-5107-8cb5-4b60bd3a4283" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323569} :answer-field/id #uuid "edf37c94-80db-5434-9531-2a778ce4fb01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e4e8ba9d-2bfa-575e-89d3-0c048e29d797" :question/math-academy-id "q-74128" :question/problem "Given the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖-2u‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n‖ku‖=|k|\\cdot ‖u‖\n$$\n\nUsing this fact and the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-2u‖ & =|-2|\\cdot ‖u‖ \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{{u}_{1}^{2}+{u}_{2}^{2}+{u}_{3}^{2}+{u}_{4}^{2}+{u}_{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{5}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{4+1+25+9+1} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{40} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{10} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323572 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "837e0fa4-b8d3-59c1-87c7-44317adafaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Constant Out of the Norm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cab7c55-f8ee-509c-830b-e0800aabaf64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323574} {:answer/id #uuid "e295f0b6-4041-514c-aae0-40e43bbbbff5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323575} {:answer/id #uuid "027afb19-f258-55dd-aac9-2c50a5e5132b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323576} {:answer/id #uuid "e07c7f34-b3b1-52c1-a378-4040827320a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323577} {:answer/id #uuid "d285f133-d909-5ada-995f-56bab6159dd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e295f0b6-4041-514c-aae0-40e43bbbbff5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323575} :answer-field/id #uuid "4956ad66-1e02-5988-8517-30f27d071a93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f19dddca-1628-5ebc-a1f1-b5fce8cd06f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-74131" :question/problem "Given the vector $w=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖-\\frac{w}{5}‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n‖kw‖=|k|\\cdot ‖w‖\n$$\n\nUsing this fact and the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-\\frac{w}{5}‖ & =|-\\frac{1}{5}|\\cdot ‖w‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{4+16+4+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323579 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "837e0fa4-b8d3-59c1-87c7-44317adafaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Constant Out of the Norm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "315838d5-27a5-5475-96eb-97269faeae49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323581} {:answer/id #uuid "76ebf912-0e85-5b3b-8ca5-09a729e3c703" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323582} {:answer/id #uuid "20f5fed7-907e-53c4-bc69-98bf8334a289" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323583} {:answer/id #uuid "0fa9927c-0d2e-52dc-8468-25f5faa4d8fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323584} {:answer/id #uuid "e14e8e7b-2f38-5b12-b0a4-4e4c04520890" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20f5fed7-907e-53c4-bc69-98bf8334a289" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323583} :answer-field/id #uuid "f849192f-9471-507c-ab82-43581ff5dd5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8294d6ba-9ce1-5c52-9203-dbd911bd55f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-74136" :question/problem "If $‖2x‖=1$, find $‖-14x‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n‖kx‖=|k|\\cdot ‖x‖\n$$\n\nUsing this fact, we can solve for the norm $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2x‖ & =1 \\\\ |2|\\cdot ‖x‖ & =1 \\\\ ‖x‖ & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $‖-14x‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-14x‖ & =14\\cdot ‖x‖ \\\\  & =14\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323586 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae41d849-9def-540c-8985-8fbeec679991" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c6de4f1-2cc8-598b-8850-0758cc849d99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323588} {:answer/id #uuid "dc674f79-0009-5dca-9636-003a0d40e527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323589} {:answer/id #uuid "e950364a-1e7b-5d59-bfe8-efc98c2a29a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323590} {:answer/id #uuid "42ec1c3e-326d-5d13-88a9-b05637d9babd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323591} {:answer/id #uuid "f4e60892-2825-5cc6-aa5b-ef03d010d37c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc674f79-0009-5dca-9636-003a0d40e527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323589} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfac79e1-c331-5ec5-ae65-03409916fc4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323587}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0e25620a-a9f8-5594-9fbe-adcb25d9df3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74138" :question/problem "Normalize the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "To normalize a vector $x,$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\frac{x}{‖x‖}.$ Therefore, to normalize $x,$ we first calculate $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4+4+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $x$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323593 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae41d849-9def-540c-8985-8fbeec679991" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fda996af-f034-58cf-9e84-9168239fd44d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323595} {:answer/id #uuid "d1080d30